<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    CONTAGION_GENOME_LIMB_AND_MATCH_BONUS_1. The owner's "plethora of organs
    AND LIMBS" (CONTAGION_GENOME_ORGAN_GROWING_1's own ruling) extended to
    real limbs. Unlike the four vanilla organs (Kidney/Liver/Lung/Heart,
    which already existed as installable ThingDefs and only needed a comp
    patched onto them), vanilla ships NO natural leg/arm ThingDef at all —
    confirmed via RimSage against the decompiled 1.6 source across every
    DLC (Core/Biotech/Royalty/Ideology/Anomaly/Odyssey): only
    SimpleProstheticLeg/Arm, BionicLeg/Arm and ArchotechLeg/Arm exist, all
    clearly artificial. So these two are new ThingDefs of our own, parented
    directly off vanilla's own BodyPartNaturalBase (Defs/Core/HediffDefs/
    BodyParts/Hediffs_BodyParts_Natural.xml) — the exact abstract parent
    Kidney/Liver/Lung/Heart themselves use — so a grown limb is
    mechanically a REAL natural body part in every sense vanilla's own
    organs are, just for Leg/Arm instead of an internal organ. Installing
    one does not add a replacement device: RecipeDefs/RM_InstallGrownLimbs.xml
    routes through vanilla's own Recipe_InstallNaturalBodyPart (confirmed
    generic to any BodyPartRecord, not organ-specific) via our
    Recipe_InstallGrownBodyPart subclass, which calls
    MedicalRecipesUtility.RestorePartAndSpawnAllPreviousParts under the
    hood — the limb is simply restored, exactly the "natural regrowth"
    tier the item's spec asked for (matching what Biotech's own Biosculpter
    Regeneration cycle does for Eye/Ear/Nose/Finger/Toe/Tongue: RESTORE, not
    replace with a device).

    <comps> here declares only the new CompProperties_GenomeMatched —
    RimWorld's XML def inheritance merges (appends) list-type fields rather
    than replacing them wholesale (confirmed against InstallNaturalKidney's
    own raw-vs-merged ingredients/fixedIngredientFilter, which show the same
    append behaviour), so BodyPartBase's inherited CompProperties_Forbiddable
    survives alongside it without being redeclared.

    ART: no queued or existing "grown limb" art found (infrastructure/
    artpipe/done/, _artsrc/ and registry.jsonl grepped by subject, all
    absent). Reuses BodyPartNaturalBase's own inherited HealthItem
    placeholder texture — the same placeholder every vanilla organ ThingDef
    (Kidney/Liver/Lung/Heart) already ships with. A dedicated icon is a fair
    follow-on, not owed by this pass.
  -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="BodyPartNaturalBase">
    <defName>RM_GrownLeg</defName>
    <label>grown leg</label>
    <description>A whole biological leg, gestated inside a Contagion amoeba from an injected genome sample. Installing it does not fit a device -- it restores the limb itself, matched to whoever the genome came from.</description>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <RecipeDef>RM_InstallGrownLeg</RecipeDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>1800</MarketValue>
      <Mass>4</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Contagion.CompProperties_GenomeMatched" />
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BodyPartNaturalBase">
    <defName>RM_GrownArm</defName>
    <label>grown arm</label>
    <description>A whole biological arm, gestated inside a Contagion amoeba from an injected genome sample. Installing it does not fit a device -- it restores the limb itself, matched to whoever the genome came from.</description>
    <descriptionHyperlinks>
      <RecipeDef>RM_InstallGrownArm</RecipeDef>
    </descriptionHyperlinks>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>1600</MarketValue>
      <Mass>3</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Contagion.CompProperties_GenomeMatched" />
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
